  "notes": "USAGE:\nCan also be written as {物真似|ものまね} in kanji. Used as a noun or with する as a verb: {物|もの}まねをする (to do an impersonation). The person who performs impersonations is called a {物|もの}まね{芸人|げいにん} or ものまねタレント.\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nImpersonation comedy is a major genre in Japanese entertainment. TV shows dedicated to {物|もの}まね are popular, and annual {物|もの}まね contests draw large audiences.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {物|もの}まねをする: to do an impersonation\n- {物|もの}まね{芸人|げいにん}: impersonation comedian\n- {物|もの}まね{番組|ばんぐみ}: impersonation show\n- {物|もの}まねが{上手|じょうず}: good at impersonations",
